{"files":[{"content":"#include <cassert>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    std::vector<int> matrix(static_cast<std::size_t>(n) * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(i) * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int windows = n - s + 1;\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    int workers = omp_get_max_threads();\n    if (workers > windows) workers = windows;\n    const bool enoughWork = n >= 256 && windows >= 64 &&\n        static_cast<long long>(windows) >= static_cast<long long>(workers) * s;\n    const int chunks = enoughWork ? workers : 1;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) num_threads(chunks) if (chunks > 1) reduction(max: mxSum)\n    for (int chunk = 0; chunk < chunks; ++chunk) {\n        const int begin = static_cast<int>(\n            (static_cast<long long>(windows) * chunk) / chunks);\n        const int end = static_cast<int>(\n            (static_cast<long long>(windows) * (chunk + 1)) / chunks);\n\n        std::vector<long long> vertical(n, 0);\n\n        // Seed this chunk's first vertical window using contiguous row reads.\n        for (int row = begin; row < begin + s; ++row) {\n            const std::size_t rowOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * n;\n            for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n                vertical[col] += matrix[rowOffset + col];\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int top = begin; top < end; ++top) {\n            long long sum = 0;\n            for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {\n                sum += vertical[col];\n            }\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n\n            for (int left = 1; left < windows; ++left) {\n                sum += vertical[left + s - 1] - vertical[left - 1];\n                if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n            }\n\n            if (top + 1 < end) {\n                const std::size_t leavingOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(top) * n;\n                const std::size_t enteringOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s) * n;\n                for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n                    vertical[col] += matrix[enteringOffset + col] -\n                                     static_cast<long long>(matrix[leavingOffset + col]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Static OpenMP work sharing over balanced top-row chunks should retain the O(N² + windows²) sliding-window algorithm while reducing fork and redundant per-thread seeding overhead when there are too few windows relative to the requested worker count.","notes":"This is a proposed experiment only; no commands or measurements were run. Added the missing standard input and OpenMP declarations reported by the previous compilation diagnostic. Chunk eligibility is derived from input dimensions and the configured OpenMP thread count.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Use an OpenMP static parallel-for over independent contiguous top-row chunks, with a max reduction for the winning sum.","Cap chunk count at the configured maximum thread count and disable parallel execution for small workloads or when chunk seeding would dominate." ]}